<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erbil</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arbil, Arbela, Hewlêr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Erbil, ancient Arbela, is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurdistan">Kurdistan</a> Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. Its citadel mound has been inhabited for thousands of years and is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>. It was an important city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>, the centre of the kingdom of Adiabene in Parthian times, and the seat of the Begteginid rulers in the 12th and 13th centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erbil.jpg" alt="Erbil" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shar_Park,_Hawler,_Erbil_Governorate,_Iraq.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
